option.ATM_CINE_SAT=Sky Saturation
option.ATM_CINE_HORIZON=Horizon Haze
option.ATM_CINE_SUNSET=Sunset Boost
option.ATM_CINE_SHADOW=Earth Shadow Blue
option.ATM_SKY_PEAK=Sky HDR Peak
option.ATM_HORIZON_TIGHT=Horizon Rolloff
option.ATM_SUN_BRIGHTNESS=Sun Disc Brightness
option.ATM_MOON_BRIGHTNESS=Moon Disc Brightness
option.ATM_SUN_GRANULATION=Sun Granulation
option.ATM_SUN_GRANULATION.comment=Convection-cell detail on the solar disc. Off makes the disc smooth.
value.ATM_SUN_GRANULATION.0=Off
value.ATM_SUN_GRANULATION.1=On
option.ATM_SUN_GRANULE_SCALE=Granule Scale
option.ATM_SUN_GRANULE_SCALE.comment=Density of the granulation cells. Higher = smaller, denser granules.
option.ATM_SUN_GRANULE_CONTRAST=Granule Contrast
option.ATM_SUN_GRANULE_CONTRAST.comment=Brightness difference between granules. Higher = more visible.
option.ATM_SUN_SPOTS=Sunspots
option.ATM_SUN_SPOTS.comment=Procedural sunspots (umbra + penumbra) on the disc.
value.ATM_SUN_SPOTS.0=Off
value.ATM_SUN_SPOTS.1=On
option.ATM_SUN_SPOT_AMOUNT=Sunspot Amount
option.ATM_SUN_SPOT_AMOUNT.comment=How much of the disc the sunspot field covers.
screen.VOLUMETRIC=Volumetric Light
screen.VL_MAIN=Basic
screen.VL_QUALITY=Quality
option.VL_ENABLED=Tyndall Effect
option.VL_ENABLED.comment=Visible sun shafts in the air where sunlight passes through cloud gaps, tree canopies or building gaps. Shares the same ray march as the underwater fog; the difference is that air scatters far less and the phase function is strongly forward, so it only shows up towards the sun.
value.VL_ENABLED.0=Off
value.VL_ENABLED.1=On
option.VL_STRENGTH=Shaft Strength
option.VL_STRENGTH.comment=Overall brightness of the shafts. Too high washes the scene out into grey haze.
option.VL_DENSITY=Air Scattering Density
option.VL_DENSITY.comment=How "hazy" the air is. Higher = more solid shafts that occlude themselves more, like foggy weather.
option.VL_PHASE=Forward Scattering Anisotropy
option.VL_PHASE.comment=Higher concentrates the shafts towards the sun (blinding when facing it, almost invisible when facing away). 0 = isotropic, shafts spread evenly.
option.VL_RAYLEIGH=Wavelength Shift
option.VL_RAYLEIGH.comment=0 = whiter (aerosol / Mie scattering, closer to a real Tyndall effect); 1 = blue (Rayleigh). Mid values give a slight blue tint.
option.VL_STEPS=Ray March Steps
option.VL_STEPS.comment=Sample count for the shafts. Higher = smoother, more expensive. Raise this first if you see noise.
option.VL_MAX_DIST=Max Distance
option.VL_MAX_DIST.comment=Furthest distance (in metres) the shafts are traced. Beyond the shadow map coverage the result is unreliable anyway, and pushing it further only adds noise.
option.INDIRECT_SPECULAR=Indirect Specular
option.INDIRECT_SPECULAR.comment=Split-sum + analytic EnvBRDF for metal/smooth-stone/gem environment reflections. Off makes them matte again.
option.SHADOW_NEAR_SHARPEN=Near Shadow Sharpen
option.SHADOW_NEAR_SHARPEN.comment=Contrast-boosts contact shadows with a smoothstep so wall/ground contact edges stay crisp, while distant shadows keep their soft edge.
value.INDIRECT_SPECULAR.0=Off (matte)
value.INDIRECT_SPECULAR.1=On (env reflections)
value.SHADOW_NEAR_SHARPEN.0=Off
value.SHADOW_NEAR_SHARPEN.1=On
option.PERF_TIER=Performance Tier
option.PERF_TIER.comment=One master switch that scales the most expensive per-pixel loops (shadow PCF / RSM bounce / screen-space reflections / underwater volumetric fog). They all cost linearly in sample count, so dropping a tier buys frame rate immediately.
value.PERF_TIER.0=Performance
value.PERF_TIER.1=Balanced
value.PERF_TIER.2=Quality
option.TM_MODE=Tonemap
option.TM_MODE.comment=Default 2 = ACES Full (Stephen Hill's full RRT+ODT fit): best highlight rolloff and colour retention. The old Narkowicz approximation has been removed. 7 = Reinhard-Jodie, harder and flatter. 3/4/6 are alternative looks.
value.TM_MODE.0=Off
value.TM_MODE.1=Reinhard
value.TM_MODE.2=ACES Full (Hill RRT+ODT)
value.TM_MODE.3=Ozius
value.TM_MODE.4=Filmic
value.TM_MODE.5=Clamp
value.TM_MODE.6=AgX
value.TM_MODE.7=Reinhard-Jodie
option.GRADE_ORANGE_SAT=Amber Saturation
option.GRADE_ORANGE_SAT.comment=Only touches the orange/amber band (hue 30 deg: skin, warm light, sunsets). The neutral grade keeps it small; 0.25-0.45 warms the image noticeably.
option.GRADE_TEAL_SAT=Teal Saturation
option.GRADE_TEAL_SAT.comment=Only touches the teal band (hue 210 deg: water, shadows). The neutral grade keeps it small and positive; a negative value suppresses cyan and makes water and shadows look muddy.
option.GRADE_GREEN_SAT=Green Saturation
option.GRADE_GREEN_SAT.comment=Only touches the green band (hue 90 deg: foliage). The neutral grade keeps it small and positive; a negative value pushes greens towards olive.
option.GRADE_GAIN=Final Soft Curve
option.GRADE_GAIN.comment=A final soft S-curve on top of the grade (Photon's gain) for a little extra punch. 1.0 = off.
