option.METEOR_MULTI_SHOWER=Annual Shower Table
option.METEOR_MULTI_SHOWER.comment=Eight real showers built in; the active one follows the simulated season.
option.METEOR_YEAR_AUTO=Advance Season Automatically
option.METEOR_YEAR_AUTO.comment=With this on the year phase advances with in-game days; off pins one season with the slider below.
option.STARS_VANILLA=Vanilla Star Texture
option.STARS_VANILLA.comment=**Off by default.** Double-images against this pack own stars; enable only for an A/B check.
value.METEOR_MULTI_SHOWER.0=Off (manual radiant)
value.METEOR_MULTI_SHOWER.1=On (8 showers/year)
value.METEOR_YEAR_AUTO.0=Off (manual phase)
value.METEOR_YEAR_AUTO.1=On (follows days)
value.STARS_VANILLA.0=Disabled
value.STARS_VANILLA.1=Enabled (A/B only)
option.GAMMA_OUT=Output Gamma
option.GAMMA_OUT.comment=Use this to brighten the whole image when it looks dim. **Higher = brighter, lower = darker.** Its advantage is that both endpoints stay pinned: pure black stays black and pure white stays white, and only the midtones are redistributed. That makes it a better tool than exposure/brightness for an image that is uniformly a little dark: brightness is a linear multiply, so raising it pushes highlights past 1.0 (clipping into flat bands) and lifts the shadows into grey. Standard sRGB is 2.2; this pack defaults to 2.35 (slightly brighter than standard).
option.GAMMA_BLACK_LIFT=Shadow Hold
option.GAMMA_BLACK_LIFT.comment=Gamma lifts the shadows more than a linear brighten does (the darker the pixel, the more it is raised). If brightening leaves the blacks washed out or makes shadow noise visible, raise this: it turns the darkest range into a linear ramp so black stays black. 0 = off.
option.SOFT_SHADOWS=Soft Shadows (PCF)
option.SOFT_SHADOWS.comment=0=hard shadow (cheaper); 1=PCF soft shadow.
value.SOFT_SHADOWS.0=Hard Shadow
value.SOFT_SHADOWS.1=PCF Soft Shadow
option.SHADOW_PCSS=PCSS Soft Shadows
option.SHADOW_PCSS.comment=0=legacy fixed-radius PCF; 1=PCSS (blocker search + penumbra estimate: sharp near, soft for floating/far occluders).
value.SHADOW_PCSS.0=Legacy PCF
value.SHADOW_PCSS.1=PCSS
option.SHADOW_BLOCKER_SAMPLES=Blocker Search Samples
option.SHADOW_BLOCKER_SAMPLES.comment=Number of taps in the PCSS blocker search. 4 is balanced; 8 is more accurate but costlier.
option.SHADOW_BLOCKER_SEARCH_TEXELS=Blocker Search Radius
option.SHADOW_BLOCKER_SEARCH_TEXELS.comment=Search radius in shadow-map texels. Larger finds distant blockers but is noisier.
option.SHADOW_SUN_ANGULAR_RADIUS=Sun Angular Radius
option.SHADOW_SUN_ANGULAR_RADIUS.comment=Controls penumbra growth. The real sun is about 0.009 rad; 0.05 is used here for visible soft shadows.
option.SHADOW_PCF_MIN_SAMPLES=PCF Minimum Samples
option.SHADOW_PCF_MIN_SAMPLES.comment=Minimum taps for the sharpest penumbra.
option.SHADOW_PCF_MAX_SAMPLES=PCF Maximum Samples
option.SHADOW_PCF_MAX_SAMPLES.comment=Maximum taps for the widest penumbra.
option.SHADOW_PCF_GAIN=PCF Sample Gain
option.SHADOW_PCF_GAIN.comment=How quickly tap count grows with penumbra radius.
option.SHADOW_DISTANCE_BOOST=Distance Softening
option.SHADOW_DISTANCE_BOOST.comment=Extra softening multiplier at distance to hide shadow-map resolution limits.
option.SHADOW_SSS=Vegetation Translucent Shadows
option.SHADOW_SSS.comment=Widens the penumbra and simulates transmission for thin geometry such as grass and leaves.
value.SHADOW_SSS.0=Off
value.SHADOW_SSS.1=On
option.SHADOW_BIAS_NEW=Distortion-Texel Bias
option.SHADOW_BIAS_NEW.comment=Uses the distortion Jacobian to scale bias to the local texel size, removing distant acne.
value.SHADOW_BIAS_NEW.0=Legacy Bias
value.SHADOW_BIAS_NEW.1=New Bias
option.SHADOW_BIAS_DISTANCE=Distance-Dependent Bias
option.SHADOW_BIAS_DISTANCE.comment=Scales the constant bias with distance (original value up close to keep contact detail, growing to 2x beyond ~30 blocks) to suppress distant shadow acne and shimmer.
value.SHADOW_BIAS_DISTANCE.0=Off
value.SHADOW_BIAS_DISTANCE.1=On
option.SHADOW_Z_COMPRESS=Shadow Z Compression
option.SHADOW_Z_COMPRESS.comment=Squeezes the shadow camera depth into a narrower range for more precision, reducing banding from long shadows at low sun. Smaller is more precise but leaves less depth headroom; 0.5 equals the previously hard-coded value.
screen.ATMOSPHERE_LIGHT=Atmosphere Lighting
option.SKY_AMBIENT=Sky SH Ambient
option.SKY_GI_REALTIME=Realtime Hemisphere Sky GI
option.SKY_GI_REALTIME.comment=High-quality tier: fires 4 hemisphere rays that query the shadow map for LARGE-SCALE occlusion (between buildings, canyons, under eaves), multiplied into the SH sky light. Small-scale occlusion is already handled by GTAO, so the two do not overlap. Cost: 4x4=16 shadow lookups per pixel.
value.SKY_GI_REALTIME.0=Off (SH only)
value.SKY_GI_REALTIME.1=On
option.SKY_GI_SAMPLES=Hemisphere Directions
option.SKY_GI_SAMPLES.comment=How many directions to sample. More = more accurate, linear cost.
option.SKY_GI_STEPS=Trace Steps
option.SKY_GI_STEPS.comment=Steps per ray. More = reaches more distant large occluders.
option.SKY_GI_REACH=Trace Distance
option.SKY_GI_REACH.comment=Furthest distance of the hemisphere rays in world units. Occluders beyond this are ignored.
option.SKY_GI_STRENGTH=Occlusion Strength
option.SKY_GI_STRENGTH.comment=How much of the realtime occlusion to mix into the pure SH result. 0 = back to pure SH.

option.SKY_AMBIENT.comment=Drive skylight and ambient from sky SH irradiance. Sunset ground turns red and shadows receive sky-colored fill.
value.SKY_AMBIENT.0=Off
value.SKY_AMBIENT.1=On
option.SKY_AMBIENT_SCALE=Sky SH Strength
option.SKY_AMBIENT_SCALE.comment=Multiplier for sky irradiance contributing to skylight.
option.AMBIENT_SCALE=Ambient SH Strength
option.AMBIENT_SCALE.comment=Multiplier for sky irradiance contributing to ambient.
option.SKY_AMBIENT_FALLBACK=Constant Fallback
option.SKY_AMBIENT_FALLBACK.comment=How much of the old constant skylight/ambient is kept when sky SH is dark.
option.SUN_TRANSMITTANCE=Sun Atmospheric Transmittance
option.SUN_TRANSMITTANCE.comment=Use atmospheric transmittance for the sun color. Sunset turns naturally red and matches sky/clouds.
value.SUN_TRANSMITTANCE.0=Off
value.SUN_TRANSMITTANCE.1=On
option.SUN_TRANSMITTANCE_GAIN=Sun Transmittance Gain
option.SUN_TRANSMITTANCE_GAIN.comment=Compensates the overall dimming from physical atmospheric transmittance while preserving red sunsets.
option.SUN_TRANSPORT=Atmosphere-Coupled Sun Colour
option.SUN_TRANSPORT.comment=Sun/moon colour becomes the transmittance through the atmosphere along the light direction at this pixel's own altitude: the whole scene reddens at the horizon, hilltops and valleys differ, and lighting shares one physics with the sky. Off falls back to the legacy empirical tint.
value.SUN_TRANSPORT.0=Legacy tint
value.SUN_TRANSPORT.1=Atmosphere-coupled
option.SUN_EARTH_SHADOW=Earth Shadow
option.MOON_LIGHT_PHYSICAL=Physical Moonlight
option.MOON_LIGHT_PHYSICAL.comment=On = geometrically derived moon irradiance (0.136*Omega_moon/pi = 2.585e-6, i.e. 1/386800 of the sun, matching the measured 0.25 lx vs 1e5 lx). Off = the legacy hand-tuned 0.05, which is 19340x (14.24 EV) too bright. NOTE: before enabling, set AUTO_EV_MIN near -23; the night sky (stars/airglow/light pollution/moon disc) is drawn at an independent artistic scale and needs rebalancing with it.
value.MOON_LIGHT_PHYSICAL.0=Legacy constant
value.MOON_LIGHT_PHYSICAL.1=Physical (geometric)

option.SUN_EARTH_SHADOW.comment=Spherical-cap solid-angle intersection gives the fraction of the sun disc still visible, a physically soft earth shadow (higher up = smaller earth disc = softer edge). Multiplied into the direct sun/moon light.
value.SUN_EARTH_SHADOW.0=Off
value.SUN_EARTH_SHADOW.1=On
option.LIGHTMAP_GAMMA=Lightmap Curve
option.LIGHTMAP_GAMMA.comment=Exponent applied to the MC lightmap (skylight g and blocklight r). 2.0 squares it: darker shadows, stronger tonal separation. 1.0 restores the old linear behaviour.
option.LIGHTING_PI=Unified 1/PI Normalization
option.LIGHTING_PI.comment=Divide the Lambert branch by PI at the end (Grafun does the same) so its magnitude matches the PBR branch and toggling PBR no longer jumps in brightness. Turn off to roll back.
value.LIGHTING_PI.0=Off
value.LIGHTING_PI.1=On
option.GROUND_BOUNCE=Ground Bounce
option.GROUND_BOUNCE.comment=Poor man's GI: sunlight hitting upward-facing ground bounces onto downward-facing surfaces (leaf undersides, eaves, bridge decks) so they no longer go pitch-black. Strength scales with solar elevation; colour follows the sun (moonlight at night).
option.LIGHTING_PBR=PBR Material Shading
option.LIGHTING_PBR.comment=Optional: Hammon diffuse + GGX specular. Off by default; the pack now uses plain Lambert N.L plus atmosphere-coupled transport.
value.LIGHTING_PBR.0=Legacy Lambert
value.LIGHTING_PBR.1=PBR
option.SPECULAR_AREA_LIGHT=Area-Light Specular
option.SPECULAR_AREA_LIGHT.comment=1=GGX specular spread over the sun/moon disc (sun radius 0.29 deg): wider, lower-peaked, more realistic. 0=point-light specular (smaller, brighter).
value.SPECULAR_AREA_LIGHT.0=Point Light
value.SPECULAR_AREA_LIGHT.1=Area Light (Decima)
option.PBR_SPECULAR_STRENGTH=Specular Strength
option.PBR_SPECULAR_STRENGTH.comment=Overall PBR specular multiplier. Too high blows out metals/smooth blocks; foliage is reduced automatically.
option.PBR_AMBIENT_SPECULAR=Ambient Specular
option.PBR_AMBIENT_SPECULAR.comment=Tiny ambient specular term so metals do not go pitch-black in shadow.
option.LIGHTING_SPECULAR=Simple Specular
option.LIGHTING_SPECULAR.comment=Adds a GGX + Schlick highlight only to metal / gem / smooth-stone blocks (not full PBR); everything else stays pure Lambert. This buys back the gold/diamond/rail look that dropping PBR would otherwise cost.
value.LIGHTING_SPECULAR.0=Off
value.LIGHTING_SPECULAR.1=On
option.SPECULAR_STRENGTH=Specular Strength
option.SPECULAR_STRENGTH.comment=Overall multiplier for the simple specular term. Too high blows out metals/gems near water.
