screen.GLASS=Glass & Translucent Blocks
option.GLASS_ENABLED=Physically Based Glass
option.GLASS_ENABLED.comment=Refraction + Beer-Lambert absorption + Fresnel + SSR for glass and ice. Off falls back to the old translucent texture blend.
value.GLASS_ENABLED.0=Off
value.GLASS_ENABLED.1=On
option.GLASS_REFRACT=Glass Refraction
option.GLASS_REFRACT.comment=Fixed screen-space offset. Translucent blocks have no own depth, so real refraction displacement cannot be computed; higher = stronger distortion.
option.GLASS_DISPERSION=Glass Dispersion
option.GLASS_DISPERSION.comment=Red/blue channels are offset in opposite directions, giving coloured fringes at glass edges. 0 = off (saves two samples); recommended for the quality tier.
option.GLASS_REFLECT=Fresnel Reflection
option.GLASS_REFLECT.comment=At grazing angles glass approaches a full mirror; looking straight through is almost pure transmission. Values above 1 exaggerate reflections.
option.GLASS_ABSORPTION=Glass Absorption
option.GLASS_ABSORPTION.comment=Beer-Lambert absorption. Stained glass derives its absorption from the texture tint; clear glass barely absorbs.
option.GLASS_THICKNESS=Glass Nominal Thickness
option.GLASS_THICKNESS.comment=Thin glass defaults to 1/16 block; ice/slime/honey use a 16x thickness. Higher = darker, more saturated body.
option.GLASS_SCATTER=Ice Internal Scatter
option.GLASS_SCATTER.comment=Ice is a scattering medium: bubbles/grain boundaries build up blue-white volumetric in-scatter, so the block stays milky even face-on. Higher = frostier; 0 = fully clear.
option.GLASS_SSR=Glass Screen Space Reflections
option.GLASS_SSR.comment=Mirror trees, buildings and terrain on screen. Hit points are re-lit with their own lighting, so night reflections stay dark.
value.GLASS_SSR.0=Off
value.GLASS_SSR.1=On
option.GLASS_SUN_DISC=Celestial Discs in Reflection
option.GLASS_SUN_DISC.comment=Adds the sun/moon disc to the glass reflection (the sky LUT stores scattered light only).
value.GLASS_SUN_DISC.0=Off
value.GLASS_SUN_DISC.1=On
option.GLASS_ICE_BUMP=Ice Surface Bump
option.GLASS_ICE_BUMP.comment=Procedurally perturbs the ice normal so refraction/reflection is no longer polished-glass smooth. Higher = rougher crystal/ melt texture; 0 = perfectly smooth.
option.GLASS_INTERNAL_BOUNCE=Internal Bounce Count
value.GLASS_INTERNAL_BOUNCE.0=Off
value.GLASS_INTERNAL_BOUNCE.1=Light
value.GLASS_INTERNAL_BOUNCE.2=Natural
value.GLASS_INTERNAL_BOUNCE.3=Thick
value.GLASS_INTERNAL_BOUNCE.4=Dense
option.GLASS_INTERNAL_BOUNCE.comment=Multiple internal reflections/refractions inside glass and ice, so light bounces within the body and the block reads as thick instead of a single film. 0 = off, 2 = natural, higher = denser (more expensive).
