screen.WATER=Water Surface
screen.WATER_SHAPE=Wave Shape
screen.WATER_OPTICS=Water Optics
option.WTR_ENABLED=Physically Based Water
option.WTR_ENABLED.comment=Enables the P1 water surface path: three-layer wave normals, refraction, Beer-Lambert absorption and sky reflection. Off falls back to the transparent background.
value.WTR_ENABLED.0=Off
value.WTR_ENABLED.1=On
option.WTR_AMP=Wave Normal Strength
option.WTR_AMP.comment=Scales the wave normal perturbation. 0 is a mirror-flat surface; values above 1 exaggerate the slopes.
option.WTR_SPEED=Wave Speed
option.WTR_SPEED.comment=Animation speed of the normal-map ripples only.
option.WTR_PATCHY=Patchy Water Energy
option.WTR_PATCHY.comment=0 makes the whole surface uniformly rippled; 1 gives broad calm/rough patches. This modulates wave amplitude, not the normal directly.
option.WTR_ABSORB_SCALE=Water Absorption Scale
option.WTR_ABSORB_SCALE.comment=Scales the red-green-blue absorption coefficients. Higher makes water murkier and shortens visibility.
option.WTR_REFRACT=Refraction Strength
option.WTR_REFRACT.comment=Screen-space refraction offset from the wave normal. Higher distorts the bottom more strongly.
option.WTR_REFRACT_DEPTH=Refraction Depth Fade
option.WTR_REFRACT_DEPTH.comment=Controls how quickly refraction settles down with view distance.
option.WTR_UNDERWATER_REFRACT=Underwater Refraction Scale
option.WTR_UNDERWATER_REFRACT.comment=Extra refraction attenuation while the camera is submerged.
option.WTR_SCATTER_DIST=Scatter Colour Distance
option.WTR_SCATTER_DIST.comment=Equivalent optical path used for the constant faint in-scatter colour.

screen.WATER_UNDERWATER=Underwater
screen.WATER_CAUSTIC_BOX=Caustics
option.WTR_FOG_FAR=Underwater Fog Reach
option.WTR_FOG_FAR.comment=Maximum visual reach of the constant underwater in-scatter colour.
option.WTR_CAUSTICS=Underwater Caustics
option.WTR_CAUSTICS.comment=Focus sunlight into a moving caustic network on underwater terrain. Only direct sunlight is affected.
value.WTR_CAUSTICS.0=Off
value.WTR_CAUSTICS.1=On
option.WTR_CAUSTIC_SCALE=Caustic Scale
option.WTR_CAUSTIC_SCALE.comment=World-space size of the caustic network. Larger values make finer cells.
option.WTR_CAUSTIC_BRIGHT=Caustic Brightness
option.WTR_CAUSTIC_BRIGHT.comment=Multiplier before the caustic power curve.
option.WTR_CAUSTIC_POWER=Caustic Contrast
option.WTR_CAUSTIC_POWER.comment=Exponent applied to the caustic pattern. Higher values make sharper, brighter filaments.
option.WTR_CAUSTIC_DEPTH_FADE=Caustic Depth Fade
option.WTR_CAUSTIC_DEPTH_FADE.comment=How quickly the caustic pattern softens with depth. Sunlight absorption is applied separately.

option.WTR_GLINT_STRENGTH=Sun Glitter Strength
option.WTR_GLINT_STRENGTH.comment=Direct GGX sun highlight on the perturbed water normal. This produces the small sparkling highlights on capillary waves.
option.WTR_GLINT_ROUGHNESS=Sun Glitter Roughness
option.WTR_GLINT_ROUGHNESS.comment=Microfacet roughness of the sun highlight. Lower values give sharper, smaller sparkles; higher values spread it into a softer sheen.

option.WTR_DELTA_NEAR=Calm Differential Radius
option.WTR_DELTA_NEAR.comment=Finite-difference spacing in calm areas. Smaller sees finer waves but is more prone to shimmering.
option.WTR_DELTA_FAR=Rough Differential Radius
option.WTR_DELTA_FAR.comment=Finite-difference spacing in rough wave patches.
option.WTR_FADE_DIST=Distance Fade Start
option.WTR_FADE_DIST.comment=Distance where the differential radius starts growing to suppress far-field shimmering.
option.WTR_FADE_MAX=Distance Fade Maximum
option.WTR_FADE_MAX.comment=Maximum extra differential radius added at long range. This is anti-aliasing, not normal flattening.

option.WTR_SSR=Water Screen-Space Reflections
option.WTR_SSR.comment=Reflects on-screen trees, terrain and structures on the water surface. Off uses only the sky LUT and sun glint.
value.WTR_SSR.0=Off
value.WTR_SSR.1=On
option.WTR_BIOME_TINT=Biome Water Tint
option.WTR_BIOME_TINT.comment=Uses the averaged biome water colour to tint the underwater in-scatter background. It does not alter the absorption coefficients.

option.WTR_GLINT_MODEL=Sun Glint Model
option.WTR_GLINT_MODEL.comment=0 = physically based GGX. 1 = Eclipse-style power-lobe approximation. Compare the highlight shape and choose the one that reads better.
value.WTR_GLINT_MODEL.0=GGX
value.WTR_GLINT_MODEL.1=Power Lobe
option.WTR_DISPERSION=Water Dispersion
option.WTR_DISPERSION.comment=Optional red/blue channel offset through the water refraction. 0 disables the extra texture samples.
value.WTR_DISPERSION.0=Off

option.WTR_GEO_SPEED=Geometric Wave Speed
option.WTR_GEO_SPEED.comment=Independent animation speed of the real displaced water geometry only. It does not affect the normal-map ripples.

option.WTR_UNDERWATER_SUN=Underwater Sun Disk
option.WTR_UNDERWATER_SUN.comment=Adds the sun disk and angular halo inside the Snell window when looking up from underwater.
value.WTR_UNDERWATER_SUN.0=Off
value.WTR_UNDERWATER_SUN.1=On
option.WTR_SHAFTS=Underwater Light Shafts
option.WTR_SHAFTS.comment=Screen-space volumetric shafts converging toward the underwater sun.
value.WTR_SHAFTS.0=Off
value.WTR_SHAFTS.1=On
option.WTR_SHAFT_STRENGTH=Light Shaft Strength
option.WTR_SHAFT_STRENGTH.comment=Intensity of the underwater volumetric shafts.
